meta {
  name: Confirm email
  type: http
  seq: 3
  tags: [
    customer
    manual
  ]
}

post {
  url: {{BASE_URL}}/api/v1/auth/confirm?token={{CONFIRMATION_TOKEN}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  token: {{CONFIRMATION_TOKEN}}
}

docs {
  No automated assertion here on purpose - this depends on a token you can only get
  from the real email SendGrid sends to CUSTOMER_EMAIL.

  Manual setup:

  1. Run "Register customer" first.
  2. Open the CUSTOMER_EMAIL inbox, find the confirmation email, and copy the token
     from the link's "?token=" query param.
  3. Paste it into the CONFIRMATION_TOKEN environment variable.
  4. Run this POST request; a 200 response means the account was activated.

  GET only shows a confirmation page and never activates the account. This prevents
  link scanners and browser prefetchers from consuming the one-time token.

  Without this step, "Login customer" returns 401: accounts start inactive
  (ativo = false) until confirmed. The token is single-use and expires after 24h.
}
